    "body": "# [AMD] GLM-5.2: use non-fused all-reduce + RMSNorm in decode on MI355X\r\n\r\n## What\r\nFor `GlmMoeDsaForCausalLM` on HIP (single node, no attention DP), also declare\r\n`disable_aiter_allreduce_fusion_in_decode=True`. Decode/verify then runs custom\r\nall-reduce followed by the fused add-RMSNorm kernel instead of the fused\r\naiter AR + RMSNorm kernel.\r\n\r\n## Why\r\nAt TP4 on MI355X the fused 2-stage AR + RMSNorm is ~10% slower than custom AR +\r\nadd-RMSNorm at every decode/verify size (16..256 tokens x 6144 hidden). An MTP\r\nverify step issues 158 of them, so AR + norm drops from 5.29 to 4.50 ms per\r\niteration at M=192.\r\n\r\n## E2E\r\nMI355X TP4, GLM-5.2-MXFP4, EAGLE MTP (3 steps, 4 draft tokens), random OSL 1024,\r\nmax running 48. Both runs use the breakable prefill graph; only the decode AR path differs.\r\n\r\n| ISL | conc | TPOT ms | output tok/s |\r\n|---|---|---|---|\r\n| 1024 | 4 | 4.08 -> 4.05 (-0.7%) | 854 -> 864 (+1.2%) |\r\n| 1024 | 64 | 13.09 -> 12.86 (-1.8%) | 3333 -> 3425 (+2.8%) |\r\n| 8192 | 4 | 4.88 -> 4.83 (-1.0%) | 738 -> 753 (+2.1%) |\r\n| 8192 | 64 | 24.74 -> 24.57 (-0.7%) | 1818 -> 1829 (+0.6%) |\r\n\r\nGeomean: TPOT -1.0%, output throughput +1.6%, TTFT -0.9%. gsm8k unchanged (0.93).\r\n\r\n## Notes\r\n- With prefill already disabled, this leaves the aiter AR fusion unused for GLM-5.2;\r\n  dropping the `enable_aiter_allreduce_fusion=True` declaration would be equivalent.\r\n- CUDA and other models are untouched.\r\n\r\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\r\n---\r\n### CI States\r\n\r\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:hourglass_flowing_sand: [Run #38496810601](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38496810601)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\r\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:hourglass_flowing_sand: [Run #38496810432](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38496810432)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\r\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [